  "verbalization": "Heparin, Bovine is associated with Disseminated Intravascular Coagulation through a chain of indications that link it to Purpura Fulminans and Ardeparin. This suggests a potential role of Heparin in the pathophysiology of Disseminated Intravascular Coagulation, possibly through its anticoagulant properties. The evidence is supported by multiple pathways, each connecting Heparin to a different intermediate entity that ultimately leads to the target condition. The shared mechanism of action—such as the inhibition of clot formation—underlines the potential relevance of Heparin in the development of disseminated intravascular coagulation. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Heparin in the cascade of events leading to this severe form of coagulopathy.",
